// Title: Service Reconnaissance Via Wmic.EXE
// ID: 76f55eaa-d27f-4213-9d45-7b0e4b60bbae
// Status: test
// Level: medium
// Author: frack113, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-02-14
// Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1047
// Description: An adversary might use WMI to check if a certain remote service is running on a remote device.
// When the test completes, a service information will be displayed on the screen if it exists.
// A common feedback message is that "No instance(s) Available" if the service queried is not running.
// A common error message is "Node - (provided IP or default) ERROR Description =The RPC server is unavailable" if the provided remote host is unreachable
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.command_line like "*_service*") and ((process.executable endswith "\\WMIC.exe") or (process.pe.original_file_name == "wmic.exe"))) and not ((((process.command_line like "*_stopservice*" or process.command_line like "*_startservice*")) or ((process.command_line like "*_Change*" or process.command_line like "*_Create*" or process.command_line like "*_Delete*" or process.command_line like "*_PauseService*" or process.command_line like "*_ResumeService*" or process.command_line like "*_SetSecurityDescriptor*" or process.command_line like "*_StartService*" or process.command_line like "*_StopService*" or process.command_line like "*_UserControlService*")))))
